Two components on the catalog page read the same query:

// NewestTab.tsx
const { data = [] } = useQuery({ queryKey: ["courses"], queryFn: fetchCourses });
const newest = data.sort((a, b) => b.publishedAt.localeCompare(a.publishedAt));

// TopRatedSidebar.tsx
const { data = [] } = useQuery({ queryKey: ["courses"], queryFn: fetchCourses });
const top = data.slice(0, 5);

The API returns the courses ordered by rating. NewestTab renders first.

Statement: "After NewestTab renders, the array TopRatedSidebar reads is in newest-first order too, because both components received the same array object from the cache."
